{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nThe plan-review Pass-3 veto `veto:cited-reference-inaccurate` (`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py`, `pass3_decide`) drops a finding whenever the Pass-2 verifier answers `cited_reference_accurate == \"no\"`. The decision rule is deterministic; the defect is in what the verifier is asked. Both plan-review verifier prompts (`src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier_agentic.md` and `plan_review_verifier.md`) say only \"for a finding that cites a specific code reference, VERIFY the citation\". When a finding's claim is that the PLAN's citation is wrong, the verifier checks the plan's citation, finds it wrong, and answers `no`, which drops the finding exactly when it is correct.\n\nEvidence from saved `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecars: all 5 drops reported on this ticket (28d0-148d x1, c159-1621 x2, 2a3d-9d00 x2) carry `cited_reference_accurate: \"no\"` together with `evidence_entails_finding: \"yes\"` and validity 0.67 to 1.0. Across all 9,757 saved sidecars the veto fired 1,489 times; 448 of those had `evidence_entails_finding: \"yes\"` and 519 had validity >= 0.5.\n\nReproduction (agentic verifier, `plan-review-verifier-agentic`, configured standard model, inside a local `gate_read_root` session): a plan fixture with the case-1, case-2 and case-4 mis-citations plus a control finding whose OWN evidence cites a wrong location. Unfixed prompt: all 3 correct findings `cra=no` and dropped; control dropped. Prompt clarified as below: all 3 `cra=yes` and surfaced; control still `cra=no` and dropped (1 sample each).\n\n## Prior intent\n\nEpic messy-moose-jig (5fd2) and the three-pass harness (`evals/plan-review-gate/harnesses/three_pass.py`) define Pass-2 as skepticism aimed at the FINDING: the verifier \"re-grounds\" the finding, and the veto is \"cited-code-reference-accuracy, ONLY when a code citation is present\" in the finding's evidence. Nothing in the epic, the kernel docs, or `docs/plan-review-gate.md` describes vetoing a finding because the plan's citation is wrong. The fix restores the documented purpose.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. Rewrite the `cited_reference_accurate` paragraph in both plan-review verifier prompts: the question tests the finding's OWN evidence references; `no` means the finding's evidence does not show what it claims; a reference the PLAN makes is not the finding's citation, so a finding that correctly reports a wrong plan citation is `yes`, never `no`.\n2. Clarify the matching decision-rule sentence in `docs/plan-review-gate.md` (the veto fires when the finding's own citation is refuted).\n3. Add a live external regression test (`tests/external/test_cited_reference_veto_scope_live.py`) that runs the agentic verifier over the reconstructed fixture: correct plan-citation findings must not be vetoed and the control must be, by majority of 3 runs. The kernel documents that verifier prompt rules are enforced behaviorally by evals, not by prompt-text greps (`review_kernel/verify.py`), so the test is behavioral and lives in the external tier.\n\nNo change to `pass3_decide`, Pass-2 verifier variance, or cross-criterion grouping. The code-review verifier prompt (`code-review-verify.md`) has similar wording but is out of scope.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The veto's decision rule is read and documented: `pass3_decide` drops on `cited_reference_accurate == \"no\"`, and the verifier prompt wording, not a location comparison in code, is what made it fire on the plan's citation (recorded in a ticket comment with sidecar evidence).\n- [ ] A regression test reproduces case 1: a plan citing nonexistent `tests/unit/test_init_ensures_seam.py`, with a G1G2 finding reporting it, is NOT dropped by the veto, while a control finding with its own wrong citation still is. The test fails on the unfixed prompt and passes on the fixed one.\n- [ ] One `review-plan` on a throwaway ticket whose plan carries the case-2 mis-citation (`CHANGELOG.md:371` for the v0.12.0 `REBAR_LLM_MODEL` removal) surfaces the citation finding instead of dropping it under the veto, or the result is recorded with its sidecar evidence.\n- [ ] All 5 recorded cases are addressed: cases 1, 2 and 4 are surfaced by the fixed verifier in the reproduction, and cases 3 and 5 share their shape (a finding correcting a plan's line citation).\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass; `tests/unit/test_criteria_vocabulary_reviewers.py`, `tests/unit/test_review_kernel.py` and `tests/unit/test_plan_review.py` pass.\n\n## Testing\n`pytest tests/unit/test_criteria_vocabulary_reviewers.py tests/unit/test_review_kernel.py tests/unit/test_plan_review.py`; the live test with `REBAR_RUN_EXTERNAL=1 pytest -m external tests/external/test_cited_reference_veto_scope_live.py` (requires provider credentials)."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793502479931698001,"uuid":"0eb47f4b-60bc-4a2c-922a-f0f4c342627b"}